        <body>
            <div xml:id="d376">

                <pb facs="d376-1" n="1" xml:id="d376-1"/>

                <head>376. Memorandum From the President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs
                    (Kissinger) to the Deputy Secretary of State (Rush), Washington, October 15,
                        1973<anchor n="1" xml:id="d376-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d376-f2"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline>
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1973-10-15">October 15, 1973</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>THE WHITE HOUSE<lb/>WASHINGTON</p>
                <p>October 15, 1973</p>
                <p>MEMORANDUM FOR</p>
                <p>THE DEPUTY SECRETARY OF STATE<lb/>THE DEPUTY SECRETARY OF DEFENSE<lb/>CHAIRMAN,
                    JOINT CHIEFS OF STAFF<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">text not
                    declassified</hi>]</p>
                <p>SUBJECT: Withdrawal of Thai Volunteer Forces from Laos</p>
                <p>After a review of the recommendations for the withdrawal of Thai SGU forces from
                    Laos, it has been decided to proceed as follows: <list>
                        <item>— During the first twenty days following establishment of the new
                            government, the RLG will notify the LPF that 13 battalions already have
                            been withdrawn and that three additional battalions will be withdrawn in
                            the initial period.</item>
                        <item>— During the next twenty day period, four additional battalions will
                            be withdrawn.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>The remaining ten battalions will begin to be withdrawn when it has been
                    determined that the North Vietnamese have withdrawn a corresponding percentage
                    (2/3) of their forces from Laos. They will then be withdrawn at a rate
                    corresponding to that of subsequent NVA withdrawals.</p>
                <p>You are requested to take appropriate action to carry out this course of
                    action.</p>
                <p>[signed] Henry A. Kissinger</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d376-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d376-f1-content">
                <p>Source: [<hi rendition="#italic">text not declassified</hi>]. Secret; Sensitive.
                    Kissinger received this memorandum under a covering memorandum, October 10, from
                    William Stearman of the NSC staff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d376-f2" n="2" xml:id="d376-f2-content">
                <p>Kissinger authorized a schedule for withdrawing Thai forces from Laos.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
